From kubernetes-ocp k376 (2026-11-06). OCP validate() now refuses the suffix of the other distribution: +k3sN under rke2 and +rke2rN under k3s; a version without a suffix stays valid. General RKE2/K3s rules belong in Rex::Rancher.

Maintainer decision (Getty, 2026-11-08, hub decision page): Rex::Rancher gets a public function release_suffix that names the distribution a version suffix belongs to (or none), documented and tested; OCP then uses it instead of its own pattern. Build after the release.
